{% from "macros.njk" import callout, snippet with context %}

{% set design %}
<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-usage">Usage</h2>
  <p>Side sheets are supplementary surfaces anchored to the left or right edge
     of the screen — M2's answer to "this content supports the screen, but
     isn't worth navigating to". Flint ships both M2 types:</p>
  <h3>Standard side sheet</h3>
  <p>Persistent and non-modal: no scrim, the page stays interactive. Use it
     for <strong>filters that control the primary content</strong>, supporting
     <strong>metadata panels</strong> (photo details, file info), or
     <strong>short configurations</strong> that stay on screen while the user
     works. Desktop and tablet only — M2 replaces it with the modal on
     mobile, and so does Flint (it is hidden below 600px).</p>
  <h3>Modal side sheet</h3>
  <p>Blocks the page behind a visible scrim and must be dismissed before the
     user can interact with the content again. On mobile it is <em>the</em>
     side sheet (M2's own rule); on larger screens it can focus attention on
     a key flow, such as a purchase or a filter-the-list moment.</p>
  <h3>Don't use it for</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Blocking decisions</strong> — confirmation and alerts are
        <a href="dialog.html">dialog</a> territory.</li>
    <li><strong>Primary navigation</strong> — that's the drawer or rail, and
        M2 explicitly pairs the side sheet on the <em>opposite</em> edge
        from the nav drawer so the two are never confused.</li>
    <li><strong>Feedback</strong> — snackbars, never sheets.</li>
    <li><strong>An inset floating panel</strong> — M2's Don't: fully insetting
        a side sheet from the edges makes its position and scroll behavior
        unclear while obscuring content. If it doesn't hug an edge, it's a
        card.</li>
  </ul>
  {{ callout({
    variant: "info",
    title: "Bottom sheets become side sheets",
    text: "When adapting for larger screens, M2 swaps bottom sheets for side sheets — same content contract, different edge. Both Flint variants share the same interior vocabulary, so the swap is a class change.",
    href: "bottom-sheet.html",
    linkText: "Bottom sheet component"
  }) }}
</section>

